  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No prior evidence exists, so the first experiment should establish a simple, interpretable baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal RNA configuration: a standard linear dimensionality reduction on a single profile with no aggregation or fusion complexity. This gives a clear floor for RNA-only performance. It is the best use of experiment 1 because (1) it isolates the RNA modality with the least confounding design choices, (2) it provides a reference point against which I can compare image-only (config_010) in experiment 2 to determine which modality carries the strongest signal, and (3) it avoids prematurely committing budget to complex multimodal or multiprofile settings before knowing whether a simple single-modality model is already competitive. Establishing this baseline first lets the remaining 9 experiments be allocated strategically toward the most promising direction."
}

